{
  "id": "calc3.multiple_integrals.reverse-order-exp",
  "course": "calc3",
  "topic": "multiple_integrals",
  "kind": "integral_setup",
  "title": "Reverse the order of integration",
  "prompt": "The integral $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\int_x^1 e^{y^2}\\,dy\\,dx$ can't be done in this order. Rewrite it with the order $dx\\,dy$ (don't evaluate).",
  "answer_format": "An iterated integral like int(int(f, y, a, b), x, c, d), inner integral first. Don't evaluate it.",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "tags": [
    "double integrals",
    "order of integration"
  ],
  "data": {
    "integrand": "e^(y^2)",
    "region": [
      [
        "y",
        "x",
        "1"
      ],
      [
        "x",
        "0",
        "1"
      ]
    ],
    "order": [
      "x",
      "y"
    ]
  },
  "answer": "int(int(e^(y^2), x, 0, y), y, 0, 1)",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Sketch the region: 0 ≤ x ≤ 1 and x ≤ y ≤ 1. It's a triangle.",
    "For a fixed y, which x-values are in the triangle?"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "The region is the triangle $0 \\le x \\le y$, $0 \\le y \\le 1$.",
    "So the integral is $\\int_0^1 \\int_0^y e^{y^2}\\,dx\\,dy$ (which then equals $\\int_0^1 y e^{y^2}\\,dy = \\frac{e - 1}{2}$)."
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "openstax-calc3",
    "section": "5.2 Double Integrals over General Regions",
    "note": "Original problem; see changing the order of integration."
  },
  "review": {
    "status": "draft"
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "name": "from a sketch",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "kind": "note",
            "content": "triangle with corners (0,0), (0,1), (1,1)"
          },
          {
            "kind": "expr",
            "content": "(e - 1)/2"
          }
        ],
        "answer": "int(int(e^(y^2), x, 0, y), y, 0, 1)"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "correct"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "swapped the limits naively",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [],
        "answer": "int(int(e^(y^2), x, y, 1), y, 0, 1)"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "incorrect",
        "hint_codes": [
          "REVERSED_LIMITS_ONLY"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "kept the old order",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [],
        "answer": "int(int(e^(y^2), y, x, 1), x, 0, 1)"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "incorrect",
        "hint_codes": [
          "INTEGRATION_ORDER"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "limit uses its own variable",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [],
        "answer": "int(int(e^(y^2), x, x, 1), y, 0, 1)"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "incorrect",
        "hint_codes": [
          "SETUP_BOUNDS"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
